### Topic 39 - Library search API (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
@base = http://localhost:8080/api/books

### All books
GET {{base}}

### One book
GET {{base}}/1

########## A. Derived query methods ##########

### findByAuthor
GET {{base}}/by-author?name=J.R.R. Tolkien

### findByTitleContainingIgnoreCase
GET {{base}}/title-contains?text=java

### findByPriceBetween
GET {{base}}/price-range?min=10&max=20

### findByGenreOrderByPriceAsc
GET {{base}}/genre/PROGRAMMING

### Invalid enum value -> 400
GET {{base}}/genre/COOKING

### findByPublishedYearGreaterThanEqualOrderByPublishedYearDesc
GET {{base}}/published-since/2010

### findTop3ByOrderByPriceDesc
GET {{base}}/top-expensive

### findFirstByOrderByPublishedYearAsc
GET {{base}}/oldest

### findByIsbn
GET {{base}}/isbn/978-0132350884

### existsByIsbn
GET {{base}}/exists?isbn=978-0132350884

### countByGenre
GET {{base}}/count?genre=FANTASY

########## B. JPQL ##########

### Keyword search in title OR author (named parameter)
GET {{base}}/search?keyword=tolkien

### Positional parameter ?1
GET {{base}}/thick?minPages=500

########## C. Native SQL ##########

### Published between two years
GET {{base}}/published-between?from=1940&to=1990

### Native GROUP BY + interface projection
GET {{base}}/stats/genres

########## E. Projections ##########

### Interface projection (only title + author are selected)
GET {{base}}/summaries?genre=HISTORY

### Dynamic projection
GET {{base}}/summaries/by-author?name=j.r.r. tolkien

### Record projection with JPQL constructor expression
GET {{base}}/stats/authors

########## Specifications & Query by Example ##########

### Any combination of filters (all optional)
GET {{base}}/filter?genre=PROGRAMMING&maxPrice=48&available=true

### Only one filter
GET {{base}}/filter?title=the

### Query by Example
GET {{base}}/example?author=martin

########## D. @Modifying (changes data!) ##########

### Raise all FANTASY prices by 10 %
PUT {{base}}/genre/FANTASY/price-factor?factor=1.10

### Delete every unavailable book
DELETE {{base}}/unavailable
